      "license": "CC BY 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0",
      "artist": "xiquinhosilva",
      "description": "Yuanmingyuan Park, located in Beijing, China, is a historic site renowned for its imperial gardens and architectural ruins. Often referred to as the Old Summer Palace, it was originally constructed in the 18th century during the Qing Dynasty as a lavish retreat for emperors, showcasing intricate landscapes and ornate structures. The park was looted and destroyed by foreign forces in 1860, leaving behind evocative remnants that now serve as a poignant reminder of its former grandeur and a symbol of cultural heritage. Today, it attracts visitors who explore its scenic lakes, scattered ruins, and restored sections, offering a glimpse into China's imperial past.",
